 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-08-30T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2137) 'the page template an RFD report is published from
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2137  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2137) 'any RFD published as a page; the PERT sheet's design system
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2137  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2137) 'Every RFD report page is published from one template in one design system.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2137  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2137) 'RFD reports published as pages have no shared shape: each one reinvents its header, its tables, and its palette.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2137  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2137) 'Copy `template.html`, fill every bracketed slot, and follow RFD66606-2134 as the worked example.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2137  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2137) 'RFD reports share one sheet
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2137  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2137) 'One template, `template.html` in this directory, in the PERT sheet's design system: Libre Franklin over IBM Plex Mono, the paper/ink/critical/done/steel tokens, light and dark themes resolved at the token level. To publish a report, copy the file, replace every bracketed slot, and keep the worked example's shape.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2137  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2137) 'Verification
 # tags: rfd:section-heading
 Text:RFD2137  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2137) 'The worked example filling the slots is RFD66606-2134, so the template is demonstrated by a report that shipped rather than by lorem.
 # tags: rfd:section
 Text:RFD2137  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2137) 'What the layout encodes
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2137  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2137) 'The layout encodes the agreements rather than describing them:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2137  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2137) '- the serial header and stamps mirror the RFD frontmatter;
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2137  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2137) '- every measurement table carries its baseline row, and the chosen row takes the green rail;
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2137  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2137) '- the figure is an inline SVG in currentColor with labelled arrows, one claim, stated again in its aria-label;
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2137  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2137) '- the retraction block is bordered in the accent and sits in place, next to what it retracts;
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2137  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2137) '- the controls card lists each planted defect the gate caught;
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2137  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2137) '- the provenance foot points at the logbook, the PRs, and the command to re-run, and pairs physical measurements with a household-object equivalent.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2137  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2137) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2137  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2137) 'The working agreements the documents encode (retractions in place, baselines beside numbers, controls named) have no slot a page reminds an author to fill.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2137  1 LINE
 Text:Written
